        "articleTitle": "The Application of Counter Techniques to Precision Frequency Measurements",
        "volume": "PGI-3",
        "issue": null,
        "startPage": "2",
        "endPage": "10",
        "publisher": "IEEE",
        "articleContentType": "Journals",
        "publicationTitle": "Transactions of the IRE Professional Group on Instrumentation",
        "authors": [
            {
                "id": 37319019300,
                "preferredName": "A. F. Boff",
                "firstName": "A. F.",
                "lastName": "Boff"
            }
        ],
        "abstract": "Principles of precision frequency measurement by use of electronic counters are discussed and limitations of frequency range extensions by the heterodyne method are outlined. A completely new frequency meter for use up to 42 mc/s is described which has the advantages of direct read-out, simple operation, and an accuracy of ± 1 part in 10<sup xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">7</sup> ± 1 c/s. Consideration is given to means of extending the frequency range into the V.H.F. and U.H.F. bands. A typical converter for the range 40 - 150 mc/s is described.",
        "keywords": {
